# {{ root_namespace }} working agreements

## 1. The topmost pin is exact

This repository has one topmost pinned mathematical package: the optional
anchor when one is supplied, or Mathlib directly when there is no anchor.
Without an anchor, Mathlib is required directly at the exact revision in
lakefile.toml. With an anchor, do not add a second independent Mathlib pin.
Never use a branch where a 40-hex commit belongs.

MathFormalContract is a named leaf dependency pinned to the same exact commit
recorded in .copier-answers.yml. It has no transitive Lake dependencies.

## 2. No sorry and no new axioms by convenience

A declaration that does not exist is an honest gap. A sorry-backed statement
is a false claim in a repository whose purpose is to be trusted. If a proof
needs a fact this environment cannot supply, record the frontier and stop.

## 3. Closed lanes are explicit

closed-lanes.json holds the positive module allowlist and each declared
closed lane. forbidden_vocabulary is checked against declarations associated
with an open frontier. Do not claim a closed lane merely because it is hard.

## 4. formalization.yaml is a claim

Every value is read by machines or by people deciding whether to trust this
repository. Unknown source coordinates stay none or pending. The bootstrap
flag is write-once and is cleared by mfc lint after the first in-scope
declaration appears.

## 5. Bind upstream theorems directly

When a source statement already has an exact Mathlib or anchor theorem, add its
fully qualified name under that registry entry's `external_decls`, with the
current `env_digest` from `attest/environment.json`. In a topic module, attach
the citation to that imported theorem:

    attribute [cites "stmt:<registry-id>:<entry-id>" (relation := exact)] Mathlib.Name

Do not add a local wrapper just to carry the citation. The generated CI step
turns the registry's external names into the emitter input, which produces
`scope: external` rows without counting them as topic declarations. Keep an
exact claim's frontier empty.

## Build and contract checks

    lake build
    lake exe emit --out attest/lean-emission.json
    mfc env --repo . --out attest/environment.json --axiom-policy attest/axiom-policy.json --emitter-version mfc-emit/1.1.0
    mfc bundle --emission attest/lean-emission.json --environment attest/environment.json --out attest/declarations.json
    mfc lint --emission attest/lean-emission.json --environment attest/environment.json --closed-lanes closed-lanes.json
    mfc check-ilean-coverage --emission attest/lean-emission.json --closed-lanes closed-lanes.json

The repository CI also validates every registry with the configured
frontier_kind_labels. A green run with not_run rules has not checked those
claims; resolve the missing evidence rather than reading the run as a pass.
